# /etc/xdg/mimeapps.list - system-scope default applications for this image.
#
# Installed by the Sublime build layer (the Dockerfile strips this comment
# block; the data lines below land verbatim at /etc/xdg/mimeapps.list, and the
# gate asserts the [Default Applications] set verbatim). This is the ONLY
# default-open mechanism: measured on kwst-probe (2026-11-20), xdg-mime /
# xdg-open and libfm (pcmanfm double-click) resolve system-wide defaults from
# here for the desktop user abc (uid 1000, HOME=/config, no user mimeapps.list),
# so NO $HOME/.config/mimeapps.list seed ships - unlike the two managed desktop
# icons (force-seed every start), a user (or session) that sets its own default
# keeps full control; per-seat override is the standard XDG chain.
#
# The type set below MUST stay 1:1 with the MimeType= line written into
# /usr/share/applications/sublime_text.desktop (same layer; the gate asserts
# both sides). libfm's "Open With" enumerates an entry for a type only when the
# entry's MimeType lists that type, hence the desktop-file expansion.
[Default Applications]
text/plain=sublime_text.desktop
application/json=sublime_text.desktop
text/x-shellscript=sublime_text.desktop
text/x-c=sublime_text.desktop
text/x-python=sublime_text.desktop
text/markdown=sublime_text.desktop
text/yaml=sublime_text.desktop
application/xml=sublime_text.desktop
text/xml=sublime_text.desktop
application/javascript=sublime_text.desktop
text/javascript=sublime_text.desktop
text/css=sublime_text.desktop
text/html=sublime_text.desktop
